          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %strong 3-groupoid
            is the next higher generalization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong 3-groupoid
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            such that all
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+pair"} parallel pair
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          %p
            Thus, up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            = succeed "-morphisms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-groupoid," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoid"} n-groupoid
          %h2#models Models
          %p
            A general 3-groupoid is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+definition+of+higher+categories"} geometrically modeled
            by a 4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+skeleton"} coskeletal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "-theorem" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+3-type"} homotopy 3-type
          %p
            A small model of this is a 3-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypergroupoid"}> hypergroupoid
            , where all
            = succeed "-fillers" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 4
            are
            %em unique
            \.
          %p
            A 3-groupoid is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+definition+of+higher+categories"} algebraically modeled
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategory"} tricategory
            in which all morphisms are invertible, and by a 3-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+Kan+complex"} algebraic Kan complex
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-strict+infinity-category"} semistrict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+definition+of+higher+categories"} algebraic model
            for 3-groupoids is provided by the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray-groupoid"} Gray-groupoid
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-crossed+module"} 2-crossed module
          %p
            An entirely strict algebraic model for 3-groupoids (which no longer models all
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+3-type"} homotopy 3-type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-groupoid"} strict omega-groupoid
